of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109524/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109632/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "1f06f515-71f0-54a6-a682-d082e002cbe1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109632/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "96d035d3-88c0-5577-97b4-f032a4184a89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109632/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5cc6ad87-8185-5275-8e54-6149c40c6b55" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109632/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "30fefb7d-7388-54cf-99dc-32fff560343a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db